  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17708276/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-aca8-678ea321340b": {
      "title": "Manager (Industry Development)",
      "description": "Manager (Industry Development) - Centre of Excellence in Maritime Safety (CEMS) | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Manager (Industry Development) - Centre of Excellence in Maritime Safety (CEMS) Fixed Terms Closing on 14 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The role of a Business Development manager at CEMS is both challenging and deeply rewarding. We are seeking individuals who not only possess comprehensive relevant knowledge and practical experience in the maritime industry but also demonstrate good communication and teamwork skills. As an industry development manager, you will play a pivotal role in shaping the Centre’s activities in line with the Maritime Technology & Research Roadmap 2026.  This position involves shaping and executing the Centre's industry engagement, research ecosystem development, and commercialisation strategy. The incumbent will serve as the primary interface between CEMS and its external stakeholders including industry partners, research institutions, institutes of higher learning, funding agencies, and international collaborators while ensuring the effective governance, project management, and business development functions of the Centre are delivered to the highest standard. What you will be working on Responsibilities: Design, develop, and implement a comprehensive framework for industry development, engagement, and outreach. Establish systematic processes for identifying, approaching, and sustaining meaningful relationships with maritime industry stakeholders including shipowners, port operators, maritime service providers, classification societies, and technology companies. Drive initiatives that translate research outcomes into practical industry applications, ensuring CEMS remains relevant, responsive, and valuable to the industry it serves. Lead the building and nurturing of a robust research ecosystem by forging strategic partnerships with industry partners, research institutes, and institutes of higher learning. Identify collaborative research opportunities, facilitate joint project development, and position CEMS as the natural convening body for maritime safety research in Singapore. Serve as the primary conduit between CEMS and its key external stakeholders and funding agencies, with particular focus on the Singapore Maritime Institute and other relevant government bodies. What we are looking for Requirements: At least 4-8 years of relevant working experience. Self-driven, independent, and possess readiness to work as a team. Ability to work in a fast-paced changing environment. People-oriented individual with good interpersonal, written, and communication skills. Strong research literacy, with the ability to critically evaluate evidence, synthesize findings from multiple sources If you meet the above requirements and are interested in this exciting opportunity, please apply with your CV and cover letter. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 14 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/18068051/005056a3-d347-1fe1-acda-b132fbe4c2be": {
      "title": "Manager (Secretariat & Planning)",
      "description": "Manager (Secretariat & Planning) | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Manager (Secretariat & Planning) Fixed Terms Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The Manager, Secretariat & Planning, will support the Registrar’s Office in overseeing key governance, secretariat, student discipline, planning and graduation-related functions at Singapore Polytechnic. The role involves coordinating complex administrative processes, supporting senior management and governance platforms, engaging a range of stakeholders, and guiding team members to ensure effective delivery of the Office’s responsibilities. What you will be working on Lead and coordinate secretariat support for key governance platforms, such as Board of Studies, Board of Governors, and relevant management committees. Plan and prepare meeting agendas, papers, minutes, submissions and follow-up actions, ensuring accuracy, timeliness and alignment with established governance protocols. Liaise with internal and external stakeholders, including Schools, Departments, MOE and other relevant parties, on Board, academic and governance-related matters. Support Board renewal and related governance processes, including coordination of documentation, communications and submissions. Provide secretariat and advisory support for student disciplinary matters, including preparation of case documentation, minutes, notifications and outcome letters. Advise on the application of student disciplinary frameworks, precedents and processes, and support reviews or refinements where required. Lead the planning and coordination of graduation ceremonies and related activities, including session planning, guest speaker nominations, scripts, procession notes and stakeholder communications. Support the Registrar and senior management in departmental planning, coordination, reporting, incident management, coordinating of visits and strategic initiatives. Supervise and guide team members to ensure effective work planning, execution, service delivery and continuous improvement. Use digital, productivity and multimedia tools to support meeting preparation, event execution, documentation and workflow efficiency. What we are looking for A university degree in any discipline. At least 4 years of relevant experience in governance, corporate secretariat, academic administration, student affairs, policy administration, regulatory compliance or related functions. Experience in an Institute of Higher Learning, public sector agency or statutory board, with exposure to supporting Boards, management committees, disciplinary processes or formal secretariat work, would be an advantage. Strong writing skills, with the ability to prepare clear, accurate and well-structured papers, minutes, letters and reports. Strong analytical, critical thinking and judgement skills, with the ability to interpret policies, frameworks and precedents appropriately. Excellent organisational, planning and coordination skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines and stakeholders. Good stakeholder engagement and communication skills, including the confidence to liaise with senior management and external agencies. Proficiency in Microsoft 365 and digital productivity tools, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Teams and AI-enabled tools. Meticulous, discreet and professional, with a strong sense of accountability and service orientation. Experience in supervising staff or leading teams would be preferred. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 16 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17964610/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-adbf-3ef32d0a340b": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Venture, Innovation & Experiential Learning)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Venture, Innovation & Experiential Learning) - School of Business | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer (Venture, Innovation & Experiential Learning) - School of Business Fixed Terms Closing on 19 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 At the Singapore Polytechnic School of Business, we believe in creating engaging and meaningful learning experiences that develop students' critical thinking, creativity, adaptability and problem-solving skills. Through applied and experiential learning, students are given opportunities to connect classroom learning with real-world business contexts and develop the confidence to take initiative and respond to new challenges. This is a hands-on academic role with a strong focus on student development, programme delivery and teaching. We are looking for someone who enjoys working with youths and is comfortable taking an active role both in and beyond the classroom. A key part of the role is to lead, plan and execute student development and entrepreneurship-related programmes, events, learning journeys, overseas programmes and other school initiatives. The appointee should be organised, adaptable, resourceful and able to take ownership of programmes from planning through to delivery, including coordinating students, colleagues, industry partners and other stakeholders, as well as managing the necessary logistics and administrative arrangements. The appointee must be competent and comfortable teaching in at least one of the following subject areas. Prior teaching experience would be advantageous: •\tBusiness foundation modules such as Marketing, Human Resource Management or Business Negotiation •\tEntrepreneurship or Innovation-related modules What you will be working on Responsibilities: Lead, plan, coordinate and execute school programmes, events, student development activities, entrepreneurship-related initiatives, learning journeys and overseas programmes, including managing the necessary logistics, budgeting, administration, documentation and coordination with internal and external stakeholders. Deliver and administer assigned modules, including teaching, learning activities and assessments. Provide pastoral care, guidance and support to students. What we are looking for Requirements: Minimum 2 years of relevant working experience and/or professional experience. Relevant qualification in Business, Entrepreneurship, Innovation or a related discipline. Strong interest in teaching and working with students, with genuine concern for their learning, development and well-being. Self-driven, adaptable and resourceful, with good time-management and problem-solving skills. Organised, responsible and able to manage multiple teaching and programme-related responsibilities. Strong team player with good interpersonal and communication skills. Experience in entrepreneurship, innovation, start-ups or the innovation ecosystem would be an advantage. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 19 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/18080716/005056a3-d347-1fe1-add8-7d5b07d842be": {
      "title": "Senior Technical Executive",
      "description": "Senior Technical Executive - School of Electrical & Electronic Engineering | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Senior Technical Executive - School of Electrical & Electronic Engineering Fixed Terms Closing on 21 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 Ranked #19 for The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers 2024 & 2025 As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. For this position, the appointee will be part of the lab management team that supports the smooth functioning of the school’s labs and to provide support to academic staff in teaching as well as supervising/guiding students in their project works whilst ensuring safety regulations are followed. Besides lab management, the appointee also has the opportunity to provide administrative and technical support to ensure smooth operation of key functional and/or project works related to the various initiatives carried out by the school. What you will be working on Responsibilities:- Support the smooth functioning of the school’s labs and assisting/conducting of lab experiments for both PET and CET courses. Provide support to academic staff in teaching as well as supervising/guiding students in their project works whilst ensuring safety regulations are followed. Undertake project/consultancy work with both internal and external stakeholders Manage stock inventory and acquire all resources necessary for the laboratories and yearly budgeting for teaching material and equipment maintenance. To liaise with vendors and evaluate quotations from suppliers for purchasing materials and lab equipment To support and assist to troubleshoot electrical/electronic/IT systems and effect minor repairs of faulty equipment of the lab facilities where necessary To housekeep lab facilities by carrying out regular lab maintenance and ensure the safety of the labs according to safety guidelines. To provide support which include coordination, consultation with various stakeholders, follow-up and implementation in school functional and/or project work. What we are looking for General Requirements:- Tertiary qualification in Electronic/Computer Engineering, or equivalent qualification in a related discipline. At least 2 years' hands-on experience working on Engineering projects. Candidates with at least 2 years of relevant working experience in one of the areas below would have an added advantage: (a) Electronics Design and Development (b) Embedded Systems (c) Computer Networking Self-driven, possess good interpersonal skills, willing to learn on the job and be a team player. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 21 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
