    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17757577/005056a3-d347-1fe1-add8-7f88d90e42be": {
      "title": "Assistant/Deputy Manager, Department of Human Resource",
      "description": "Assistant/Deputy Manager, Department of Human Resource | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Assistant/Deputy Manager, Department of Human Resource Fixed Terms Closing on 20 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 As Singapore's first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is as a polytechnic for all ages, we prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready, and world ready for the transformation of Singapore. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. What you will be working on Learning & Capability Development Drive the implementation of learning and development programmes, including end-to-end coordination and delivery, while supporting the review and enhancement of learning frameworks, curriculum, and capability development initiatives to ensure alignment with organisational needs. Leadership Development & 360 Feedback Exercise Support the design and delivery of leadership development initiatives, including coordinating organisation-wide 360 feedback exercises (e.g. LCF360) and supporting follow-up interventions to strengthen leadership effectiveness. Staff Sponsorship Programmes Manage the end-to-end administration of staff sponsorship programmes for academic studies, including application processing, stakeholder engagement, communications, record management, reporting and policy review. Support the enhancement of related policies, processes and guidelines to ensure effective programme delivery and governance. Career Development Initiatives Support the design and implementation of career development initiatives, including programmes that promote career fitness and employee ownership of development, to strengthen workforce readiness and mobility. Learning Analytics, Dashboards & Reporting Prepare operational reports and maintain dashboards to track key learning metrics, providing regular updates to support programme monitoring and continuous improvement. What we are looking for At least 3 years' experience in HR, with relevant experience in L&D, HR, or programme management Familiarity with Public Sector Human Resource policies, practices and guidelines will be an advantage Demonstrate excellent communication, stakeholder management, and problem-solving abilities, complemented by strong attention to detail A collaborative team player who is proactive, resourceful and confident IHRP certification preferred Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 20 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
