    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/18086716/005056a3-d347-1fe1-ae8a-ab0d3236a2bf": {
      "title": "Deputy Manager, Programme Innovation & Solutions",
      "description": "Deputy Manager, Programme Innovation & Solutions - PACE | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Deputy Manager, Programme Innovation & Solutions - PACE Fixed Terms Closing on 23 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 Singapore Polytechnic's Professional and Adult Continuing Education (PACE) Academy champions lifelong learning and skills mastery. We offer Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes that help adult learners remain employable and industry-relevant, and we partner enterprises to strengthen workforce capabilities through training, workplace learning and consultancy solutions. Reporting to the Senior Manager (Programme Innovation & Solutions), you will design, pilot, scale and evaluate skills-based CET and workplace learning solutions that support workforce upskilling and enterprise transformation. Working with course teams, industry partners and public agencies, you will translate labour-market and job-skills insights into relevant learning solutions, provide pedagogical guidance, and apply artificial intelligence (AI), learning technologies and data analytics responsibly to improve learning design, facilitation, assessment, learner support and programme outcomes. What you will be working on Responsibilities: - Analyse labour-market trends, job roles, work tasks, skills gaps, learner profiles and enterprise needs using qualitative and quantitative evidence. Translate identified needs into competency-based learning outcomes, modular pathways, authentic workplace tasks and assessment strategies for new or refreshed CET offerings. Develop and evaluate business cases, programme concepts and fit-to-purpose training, micro-credential, workplace learning and performance-support solutions. Provide evidence-informed pedagogical and andragogical guidance to course teams on blended, online, micro-learning and workplace-integrated learning approaches. Design and pilot responsible AI-enabled approaches for content development, learner support, feedback, skills assessment and learning analytics, with appropriate human oversight. Guide course teams on effective prompting, AI-output verification, bias and hallucination checks, data privacy, intellectual property, accessibility and transparent AI use. Manage NACE@SP workplace learning courses, mentorship support projects and enterprise transformation projects from scoping and proposal development to delivery, evaluation and closure. Maintain project governance across scope, schedule, budget, resources, risks, deliverables, funding requirements and benefits realisation; use feedback and outcome evidence to drive continuous improvement. Build productive relationships with SWDA, NACE Centres, IHLs, industry partners, corporate clients, adult learners, adjunct educators, consultants and internal stakeholders. Use dashboards, learning analytics and performance data to monitor adoption, quality, risks and outcomes, and present concise, decision-ready recommendations to stakeholders. What we are looking for Requirements: - Competent in learning and development, e.g. learning solution design, workplace learning solution design, curriculum design, technology-enabled learning delivery. At least 5 years of relevant experience in CET, adult learning, curriculum or learning solution design, workplace learning, learning technology, consulting or project delivery. Demonstrate ability to conduct learning-needs and job-task analysis and design competency-based curricula, authentic assessments and workplace learning solutions. Practical digital and generative AI literacy, including effective prompting, evaluation of AI outputs and responsible use of AI in teaching, learning, assessment or content workflows. Sound understanding of adult learning, learning technologies, data literacy, accessibility, data privacy and intellectual property considerations. Strong project, risk and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to facilitate co-design, influence decisions and manage multiple priorities. Strong analytical, business writing, presentation and interpersonal communication skills; able to convert evidence into clear recommendations. Learner- and client-centred, ethical, inclusive, collaborative, resourceful and comfortable experimenting, learning and sharing practice. Relevant certifications or work samples in adult education, workplace learning, project management, data analytics or AI-enabled learning will be advantageous. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 23 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17565358/005056a3-d347-1fe1-aeef-420e607c62bf": {
      "title": "Senior/Lead Research Engineer",
      "description": "Senior/Lead Research Engineer | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Senior/Lead Research Engineer Fixed Terms Closing on 27 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 Ranked #19 for The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers 2024 & 2025 The Centre of Excellence in Maritime Safety (CEMS) is a national R&D centre, a collaborative effort between Singapore Polytechnic and the Singapore Maritime Institute. We focus on developing innovative digital solutions and training systems to enhance maritime safety. Our state-of-the-art research facilities, including South-east Asia's first navigation research simulator, setting us as an innovation champion. You will join CEMS as a Senior AI Engineer/Lead and play a key role in developing applied AI solutions for real-world use cases across training, assessment, operations, research, and digital transformation. The role requires strong hands-on experience in computer vision and/or speech recognition, with the ability to design, develop, evaluate, and deploy AI models. You will work on centre-level AI projects and may also contribute to department- and school-level AI initiatives involving broader AI adoption across R&D, operations, and education. As a senior member of the team, you will also supervise and guide AI engineers, support project planning, and ensure technical delivery across multiple AI workstreams. What you will be working on Responsibilities Design, develop, and implement AI models and pipelines for real-world applications in training, assessment, safety, operations, and decision-support. Develop AI solutions involving video analytics, object detection, image classification, visual attention analysis, speech-to-text, audio processing, communication analysis, and related applied AI tasks. Work with data from video, audio, sensors, simulators, operational systems, and other sources to develop AI-enabled analytics and assessment capabilities. Integrate AI models with software platforms, dashboards, simulators, sensor systems, training platforms, or decision-support tools to support practical deployment and operational use. Explore, evaluate, and prototype suitable AI techniques, including deep learning, sequence models, multimodal learning, natural language processing, and large language model applications where relevant. Lead AI components within R&D projects, manage technical milestones, prepare documentation, and ensure timely delivery of project outputs. Supervise and mentor AI engineers or junior team members, review technical approaches, guide model development, and support capability building within the AI team. Work with internal teams, academic staff, industry partners, and external stakeholders to co-develop AI solutions and apply AI capabilities across centre-, department-, and school-level initiatives. Present AI approaches, findings, prototypes, and project outcomes to management, project partners, and industry collaborators in a clear and practical manner. What we are looking for Qualifications Tertiary Qualification in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Computer Engineering, Data Science, or a related field. Strong hands-on experience in computer vision and/or speech recognition, including model development, training, evaluation, and deployment. Relevant technical experience may include video analytics, object detection, image classification, pose or behaviour recognition, visual attention analysis, speech-to-text, audio processing, speaker or communication analysis, natural language processing, or multimodal AI involving video, audio, sensor, simulator, or time-series data. Proficiency in Python and experience with AI/ML frameworks and toolkits such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, OpenCV, Hugging Face, or equivalent. Strong understanding of machine learning and deep learning model development, including data preparation, model training, evaluation, optimisation, and performance validation. Experience integrating AI models into software systems, dashboards, simulators, training platforms, or operational applications is preferred. Experience with Large Language Models (LLMs) is an added advantage, particularly in applications beyond standard chatbot or document Q&A systems, such as multimodal AI, speech/video understanding, automated assessment, structured information extraction, model evaluation, fine-tuning, or integration with operational software systems. Experience leading AI workstreams, supervising technical staff, or mentoring junior engineers is preferred. Strong problem-solving ability, project execution skills, communication skills, and ability to work with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 27 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17481550/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-afa1-c81f3fc8340b": {
      "title": "Learning Solutions Technologist, Dept of Educational Development",
      "description": "Learning Solutions Technologist, Dept of Educational Development | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Learning Solutions Technologist, Dept of Educational Development Fixed Terms Closing on 28 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 Ranked #19 for The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers 2024 & 2025 As Singapore's first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is as a polytechnic for all ages, we prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready, and world ready for the transformation of Singapore. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. What you will be working on You will work with a team of Learning Solutions Technologists to implement EduTech-related projects within Singapore Polytechnic. You will also be involved in the management of enterprise EduTech systems such as Learning Management System and Learning Analytics platforms and provide technical solutions to meet end-users’ teaching and learning requirements. This role will also give you an opportunity to collaborate with other technologists in other polytechnics on joint initiatives to enhance EduTech-enabled Teaching and Learning. Responsibilities:- Manage and/or support the end-to-end implementation and daily operations of enterprise EduTech-related project, including procurement, system implementation, service improvements, issue tracking and resolution, and technical support. Conceptualize, and implement process and operational enhancements for EduTech platforms to increased productivity and to meet stakeholder requirements. Conceptualize and lead implementation EduTech projects (proof-of-concepts, scale-up etc.) Provide technical solutioning for end-users, i.e. academic staff, which includes user requirements gathering, identification of business needs, and proposing solutions to meet the requirements. Exploration of new technologies to support SP’s key teaching and learning (T&L) initiatives including working with other institutes of higher learning on joint exploration projects on new T&L technologies. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. What we are looking for Relevant qualifications in Computer Science, Engineering, or Information Systems or equivalent Minimally 4 years of experience in the area of project management, procurement, implementation and management of enterprise-wide systems, preferably in a Civil Service/Public Service setting Able to work in an environment using Cloud systems Fluent in a variety of programming languages, software, and systems Competent computing and scripting skills Passion and interest in technologies especially EduTech Strong analytical and problem-solving ability Strong interpersonal skills to engage with all levels of staff, including senior stakeholders to bridge user requirements and technical solutions Strong communication skills (written and spoken) Ability to multi-task and work within tight deadline Ability to work both independently and in a team Detail-oriented and highly organised Knowledge and experience with the following would be an advantage: Managing EduTech or Learning Analytics systems for an institution of higher learning AWS services (Bedrock, SageMaker, Athena, RDS, ECR, ECS, EMR, Lambda, Redis, etc.). Building and maintaining data pipelines, data wrangling and working with structure and unstructured datasets. Developing and implementing AI applications, prototypes or POC using Large Language Models. Sound knowledge of government security policy and compliance guidelines Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 28 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
    },
