    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17842877/005056a3-d347-1fe1-b29a-bde21af682c3": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Cybersecurity)",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Cybersecurity) | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Cybersecurity) Fixed Terms Closing on 14 Nov 2026 Applications for this job will be unavailable from SGT 00:00AM - 12:00PM on 17/10/2026. Please save this job and apply later. Currently unavailable Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic is challenging and meaningful. Not only must he/she possess the relevant knowledge and industry experience, he/she must also possess the ability to deconstruct the knowledge and experience, guiding students to reconstruct them as their own knowledge. He/she must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing them, and moulding their characters. There will be opportunities to develop the curriculum, introduce new courses as well as be involved in consultancy and other applied research projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/Institutional strategic initiatives will be an important part of the job too.  Successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful, innovative, proactive, and possess good communication skills. What you will be working on Cybersecurity The appointee should possess expertise in at least one area and demonstrate the ability and willingness to develop capabilities in other cybersecurity domains: Secure Coding Applied Cryptography Industrial Control Systems (ICS) / Operational Technology (OT) Security Malware Reverse Engineering Ethical Hacking and Defences IoT and Cloud Security Responsibilities:- Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials, and facilitate learning of students (youths and adult learners) Develop and maintain new/existing teaching curriculum.  This includes regular review of existing curriculum and make recommendations on areas for improvement that would enhance students’ learning, performance and employability. Keep abreast of trends and developments in cybersecurity Support the School's strategic initiatives through involvement in committee work and projects such as process improvement projects, development and management of new courses What we are looking for Requirements:- Minimum 2 years of relevant industry experience in cybersecurity, software development, IT infrastructure, cloud computing, systems engineering, network engineering, digital forensics, or related technology domains. Candidates with a strong technical foundation and an interest in developing expertise in cybersecurity are encouraged to apply. Passionate about education and possess strong interest in teaching and mentoring both youths and adult learners. Self-driven, independent, and able to work effectively as part of a team. Familiarity with Linux and Windows environments. Familiar with cybersecurity principles, IT security best practices, and common security standards or frameworks (e.g. NIST, CIS Controls, ISO 27001). Possess programming, scripting, automation or software development experience in at least one language (e.g. Python, JavaScript, Java, C/C++, PowerShell). Membership in a recognised information security or cybersecurity professional body will be an advantage. Relevant cybersecurity certifications (e.g. CISSP, CISA, CISM, OSCP, Security+, CEH, QISP or equivalent) will be an advantage. We welcome applications from IT and Computer Science professionals, including early-career candidates, who possess strong technical aptitude and an interest in developing a career in cybersecurity education. Training and professional development opportunities will be provided to support capability development. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Currently unavailable Save About your application process This job is closing on 14 Nov 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
