ey Responsibilities: Partner business units to understand their priorities, assess current and future workforce needs, and provide advisories. Manage recruitment activities, including talent sourcing, candidate assessment, offer management and appointment, to support timely and quality hiring outcomes. Advise managers and employees on HR policies, workforce matters and employee relations, supporting the fair, consistent and timely resolution of workplace issues. Support performance and talent management processes by guiding managers, facilitating constructive conversations, and identifying development and succession needs. Work with business units and HR colleagues to support employee engagement, organisational change and key employee lifecycle activities, contributing to a positive employee experience. Analyse workforce data and trends to provide actionable insights and collaborate with stakeholders on HR projects and process improvements that strengthen service delivery and organisational effectiveness. What we are looking for Requirements: At least five years of relevant HR experience, preferably with strong exposure to HR business partnering, recruitment, performance management and employee relations. Sound knowledge of HR principles and practices, with the ability to translate policies into practical guidance for managers and employees. Familiarity with Public Sector human resource policies, practices and guidelines will be an advantage. Excellent communication, stakeholder management and problem-solving skills, with the confidence to engage stakeholders at different levels. Strong analytical, organisational and project management abilities, complemented by attention to detail and sound judgement. A collaborative and service-oriented team player who is proactive, resourceful, adaptable and able to manage multiple priorities effectively. IHRP certification is preferred. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Currently unavailable Save About your application process This job is closing on 12 Nov 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
