ng in PET and CET courses) as well as school’s initiatives and activities. Build capabilities in sustainability and establish a network of strategic partnerships with government agencies, training providers, industry associations and other relevant stakeholders to support PET, CET and IE. Develop and sustain the CLS alumni community, driving engagement initiatives that deliver measurable outcomes aligned with organisational priorities in lifelong learning and student success. What we are looking for Relevant qualifications in STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics) or sustainability-related field of studies. At least 2 years of relevant working experience in Nutrition, Exercise Science, Chemistry, Environmental/Chemical Engineering, Food Science, Environmental Sustainability or Biotechnology. Have experience in engaging internal and external stakeholders to drive initiatives and maintain a good rapport and relationship with these stakeholders and alumni. Passionate about education and possess strong interest in guiding PET and CET students. Self-driven, independent, constructive and work well as a team. People-oriented individual with strong interpersonal, written and communication skills. Keen interest to develop new capabilities through projects and self-directed learning. Technologically proficient, with strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications (PowerPoint and Excel), the use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools for work (such as Claude, Copilot 365, etc), and social media platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, TikTok and LinkedIn. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Currently unavailable Save About your application process This job is closing on 12 Nov 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
