      "title": "Senior Executive/ Assistant Manager",
      "description": "Senior Executive/ Assistant Manager - Dept of Student Development | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Senior Executive/ Assistant Manager - Dept of Student Development Fixed Terms Closing on 11 Nov 2026 Applications for this job will be unavailable from SGT 00:00AM - 12:00PM on 17/10/2026. Please save this job and apply later. Currently unavailable Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The Senior Executive / Assistant Manager, Student Development supports the department in student club management, systems administration, facilities management and student club finance administration. The role works closely with students, staff, vendors and stakeholders to ensure smooth operations and service delivery, while supporting departmental projects, events and continuous improvement initiatives. What you will be working on 1. Club Management & Student Development Manage assigned CCA clubs and guide student leaders on club administration, programmes, leadership development and succession planning. Review club matters, identify issues and work with relevant stakeholders to resolve them. 2. Facilities Management Manage sports facilities bookings, utilisation, maintenance coordination and operational readiness. Manage outsourced administrative and facilities support services, including procurement, vendor coordination and related documentation. 3. Student Systems Administration Administer student development systems, including user access, enquiries, reporting and operational matters. Coordinate system enhancements, testing and continuous improvement initiatives. 4. Student Club Finance Administration Administer claims, reimbursements and advances for student clubs, ensuring compliance with financial policies and approved budgets. Resolve financial issues with Finance and relevant stakeholders, and identify ways to streamline finance administration processes. What we are looking for Recognised degree or equivalent professional qualification. At least 2 years of relevant working experience in administration, operations or a related area, with experience in handling stakeholders and operational matters. Experience in facilities management, procurement, vendor management and/or systems administration would be advantageous. Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, with good analytical and problem-solving abilities. Comfortable working with systems, data and operational processes. Resourceful, able to work independently, take ownership of issues and manage multiple priorities effectively. Passionate about student development and working with youths. Currently unavailable Save About your application process This job is closing on 11 Nov 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and cont