      "description": "Lecturer - School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer - School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering Fixed Terms Closing on 08 Nov 2026 Applications for this job will be unavailable from SGT 00:00AM - 12:00PM on 17/10/2026. Please save this job and apply later. Currently unavailable Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic is challenging and meaningful. Not only will he/she has both the knowledge and working experience, he/she must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing and moulding their characters. The successful candidate will be expected to play a critical role in curriculum development, pedagogy innovation and participation in applied research projects.  There will be opportunities to introduce new courses as well as be involved in consultancy projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/Institutional strategic initiatives will be an important part of the job.  The successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful and innovative with initiative and good communication skills. What you will be working on Responsibilities: - Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials and mentoring of students Develop and maintain new/existing teaching curriculum modules Undertake projects/consultancy work with both internal and external stakeholders Deploy effective pedagogy to facilitate learning General Requirements: - Passionate about education and possess strong interest in teaching and mentoring students Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team People-oriented individuals with strong interpersonal, written and communication skills Candidates who possess experience in teaching will have an added advantage Keen interest to develop new capabilities through projects and self-learning Possess strong interest in exploring new technologies Contribute to the teaching of the Professional Adult and Continuing Education (PACE) classes conducted at night. What we are looking for Additional Requirements (Lecturer –Rapid Transit Technology): Competent to teach at Diploma and higher levels in one of the following areas: - Rapid Transit Signalling System - Rapid Transit System - Engineering Data Analytics and Industrial Internet of Things - Engineering Asset Management & Operation Technology Possess 3 years of relevant working experiences in one of the above areas. Additional Requirements (Lecturer –Power and Sustainable Energy): - Competent to teach at Diploma and higher levels in one of the following areas: (a) Building Energy Efficiency & Management (b) Electrical Power systems & Installation (c) Power Electronics & Drives (d) Energy Storage Systems Possess 3 years of relevant work experience in one of the above areas Candidate who is currently a Professional Engineer (PE) or in the process of becoming a PE would have an added advantage. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Currently unavailable Save About your application process This job is closing on 08 Nov 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
