    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/18132585/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b184-49460ba8b40b": {
      "title": "Data Governance Specialist",
      "description": "Data Governance Specialist | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Data Governance Specialist Fixed Terms Closing on 08 Nov 2026 Applications for this job will be unavailable from SGT 00:00AM - 12:00PM on 17/10/2026. Please save this job and apply later. Currently unavailable Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The appointee will manage a broad portfolio of governance, administrative and operational functions within INDT. The role will work closely with the SP Chief Data Officer to drive data governance, IM8 and Whole-of-Government compliance; oversee data-sharing requests; managing departmental budgets and records; and leading secretariat and coordination support for management committees and IT Disaster Recovery activities. The appointee will also identify and implement digitalisation and process improvements through the effective adoption of Whole-of-Government productivity and automation tools. What you will be working on Partner the SP Chief Data Officer in driving data governance and Whole-of-Government compliance, providing sound advice to stakeholders on requirements, risks and appropriate controls. Oversee inter-agency data-sharing requests and engage Data Owners and stakeholders to ensure robust, compliant and timely review and approval. Lead the development, implementation and continuous improvement of data governance standards, templates, guidance and knowledge resources aligned with organisational and Whole-of-Government requirements. Manage departmental budgets, records and information governance, exercising oversight of budget performance, access controls, filing structures and compliance obligations. Lead secretariat and coordination support for management meetings, committees and IT Disaster Recovery activities, ensuring decisions, risks and follow-up actions are properly documented and tracked to completion. Identify, evaluate and implement digitalisation and process improvements using Whole-of-Government productivity and automation tools, while guiding stakeholders in effective adoption. What we are looking for At least five years of relevant professional experience in data governance, IT governance, corporate administration, project coordination or a related function, preferably with demonstrated ownership of complex initiatives and stakeholder engagement. Strong working knowledge of data governance, data-sharing, information management, compliance and risk-management principles, with the ability to apply them in complex operational settings. Demonstrated experience in budget administration, records management, secretariat support and the coordination of management committees or cross-functional initiatives. Strong analytical, organisational and problem-solving skills, with sound judgement and the ability to manage competing priorities, resolve issues and drive actions to completion. Excellent written and verbal communication and stakeholder-management skills, with the ability to influence, facilitate discussions and explain governance and compliance requirements clearly. Meticulous, self-driven and able to work independently with minimal supervision, while building effective working relationships across departments and with external stakeholders. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Currently unavailable Save About your application process This job is closing on 08 Nov 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
