    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/16993194/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b1e8-78dfbfd0f40b": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - School of Mechanical and Aeronautical Engineering | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer - School of Mechanical and Aeronautical Engineering Fixed Terms Closing on 12 Nov 2026 Applications for this job will be unavailable from SGT 00:00AM - 12:00PM on 17/10/2026. Please save this job and apply later. Currently unavailable Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026. Shape the Engineers of Tomorrow Robotics and automation are no longer the future. They are the present. As industries accelerate their transformation, the engineers who will lead this change are sitting in classrooms today. We are looking for an educator who is ready to inspire them. The School of Mechanical and Aeronautical Engineering is seeking a Lecturer in Mechatronics & Robotics, someone who brings both technical depth and a genuine passion for teaching, and who wants their work to matter beyond the classroom. What you will be working on What You Will Do This is a role with real breadth and real impact. You will design and deliver courses for full-time students, adult learners, and industry professionals, bringing the realities of modern manufacturing into every lesson. You will mentor students through their academic journeys and support their growth as both engineers and individuals. Beyond teaching, you will stay at the forefront of your field through applied research and consultancy, collaborate with industry partners to create meaningful learning experiences, and contribute to curriculum and institutional initiatives that keep our courses relevant and forward-looking. What You Will Teach You should be competent in one or more of the following areas: Robotics and Automation. Programmable Logic Controllers (PLC). 2D/3D Computer-Aided Drafting (CAD). C/C++ or Python Programming. What we are looking for What You Bring A tertiary qualification in Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related discipline is required. We value at least two years of relevant industry experience in areas such as automation, manufacturing, or Industry 4.0, though we warmly welcome fresh graduates who bring strong technical foundations and a clear commitment to education. What We Offer You will join a school that values both technical excellence and human development. Here, you will have the space to keep your hands on the tools through research, consultancy, and industry collaboration, while building a career as an educator who makes a lasting difference. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Currently unavailable Save About your application process This job is closing on 12 Nov 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
    },
