      "title": "Executive / Senior Executive",
      "description": "Executive / Senior Executive - Dept of Communications | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Executive / Senior Executive - Dept of Communications Fixed Terms Closing on 21 Nov 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The appointee will play an active role in supporting SP’s outreach and engagement strategies under the Department of Communications. He/she will work closely with internal schools and departments, as well as external partners such as secondary schools, educators and other stakeholders, to plan and deliver outreach activities that strengthen awareness of SP’s programmes and enhance engagement with prospective students and their influencers. What you will be working on Manage and strengthen partnerships with secondary schools through education and career guidance activities, including school roadshows, talks and learning journeys. Support key outreach events and engagement platforms involving prospective students, parents and educators, including First Steps and Open House. Plan, coordinate and support SP’s academic schools to support and facilitate their outreach programmes and stakeholder engagement activities. Plan, coordinate and support international student outreach and recruitment initiatives aimed at increasing international student enrolment. Manage the recruitment, training and deployment of SP student ambassadors to support outreach activities effectively. What we are looking for Relevant qualification in communications, marketing, education, business or a related discipline. Excellent command of spoken and written English, with good interpersonal and communication / stakeholder engagement skills to engage students, parents, educators and internal stakeholders professionally. Strong organisational and coordination skills, with the ability to manage multiple outreach activities, events and stakeholders. A collaborative team player who is comfortable working with academic schools, departments and external partners. Prior experience in outreach, events, student engagement, education marketing or stakeholder management would be an advantage. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 21 Nov 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
