    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17579935/005056a3-d347-1fe1-b2ff-53b110fea2c3": {
      "title": "Senior Executive (Finance)",
      "description": "Senior Executive (Finance) – PACE Academy | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Senior Executive (Finance) – PACE Academy Fixed Terms Closing on 14 Nov 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 Singapore Polytechnic's Professional and Adult Continuing Education (PACE) Academy is a leading continuing education and training (CET) academy that advocates the pursuit of lifelong learning and skills mastery. We offer a wide range of training programmes for adult learners to enhance their employability, and partner the industry closely in workforce development. Reporting to the Manager or equivalent, the Finance role is part of the PACE Finance team focused on executing finance and accounting operations in PACE Academy. What you will be working on Responsibilities:- Budget and Grant Management Coordinate budget preparation, forecasting and budget review exercises. Monitor budget utilisation, grant balances and funding availability. Process grant claims, disbursements, journals and related financial transactions. Monitor purchase commitments and budget utilisation. Financial Reporting and Reconciliation Prepare financial reports, dashboards and supporting analyses. Assist in variance analysis and management reporting. Perform grant reconciliations and investigate discrepancies. Support year-end closing, accruals and financial reporting activities. Compliance, Audit and Stakeholder Support Support compliance with grant conditions, SP policies and financial regulations. Maintain audit trails and supporting documentation. Support internal and external audits. Liaise with stakeholders on budget, funding and grant-related matters Support process improvement initiatives. What we are looking for Requirements:- Preferably 3 to 5 years of relevant experience in budgeting, grant management, finance operations, management reporting or financial analysis Experience in grant administration, public sector funding, education institutions or government-funded programmes is preferred Experience in audit, compliance or financial governance will be advantageous Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Good understanding of budgeting, forecasting and financial reporting Knowledge of grant administration and compliance requirements Proficiency in advance Microsoft Excel and financial systems such as Workday Strong communication and stakeholder management skills Meticulous, organized and able to manage multiple priorities independently Comfortable working in a fast-paced and dynamic environment, balancing multiple grants, budgets, reporting requirements and ad hoc requests concurrently Strong ability to adapt to changing business needs, funding requirements and operational priorities Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 14 Nov 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
