trends. The appointee must be competent to teach in the following related subjects: •\tThermofluids •\tFluid Mechanics •\tEngineering Thermodynamics •\tIntroduction to Sustainability Reporting and Strategies What you will be working on Responsibilities:- Provide administrative support in the running of the diploma course and general school operations Collaborate with industry to enhance students’ learning through activities such as industry field trips, student-industry projects, internship program and overseas programme Develop modules and conduct both industry-relevant full-time and part-time courses for internal stakeholders, students and industry personnel Inspire, facilitate and guide students through effective learning activities Serve as a personal tutor, providing pastoral care for students Organise outreach activities What we are looking for Requirements: Relevant work experience in thermal systems and Sustainability Development related field. Good oral and written communication skills Self-driven and independent team player Passionate about education and possess a strong interest in teaching and mentoring both young adults and adult learners Relevant qualifications in the field of Mechanical Engineering/Building Services/Facility Management/Sustainability Engineering or related areas of study Applicants with an ISO Lead Auditor Certification will be advantageous. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 19 Nov 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. W